<newsitem itemid="250750" id="root" date="1996-12-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: UBS sets warrant on China-related stocks.</title>
<headline>UBS sets warrant on China-related stocks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland, Hong Kong Branch, said it is issuing 180 million American style call warrants on a basket of China-related shares.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p> CITIC Pacific Ltd		     0.1 shares</p>
<p> Guangdong Investment Ltd	    0.5 shares</p>
<p> Guangnan (Holdings) Ltd	     0.3 shares</p>
<p> Guangshen Railway Co Ltd	    0.6 shares</p>
<p> Guangzhou Investment Co Ltd	 0.7 shares</p>
<p> Ng Fung Hong Ltd			0.3 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	HK$13.0666   PREMIUM	 11.01 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.3998    GEARING	 3.85X</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  11.DEC.97    PAYDATE	 2 WKS AFTER LAUNCH</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG    MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE    HK$15.3725</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
